Who are you to deal with us, Jesus of Nazareth? Have you come to destroy us? I know who you are: the Holy One of God!
Jesus said firmly, "Be quiet!" "Come out of him!"
The evil spirit violently shook the man. Then it came out of him with a scream.
We were all astonished. We even asked each other, "Who is he? What is this? A new teaching! And with such authority! Even to command evil spirits and they obey him."
The news about Jesus spread rapidly throughout Galilee. Jesus heals many people.
Jesus and those with him went out of the mosque. Immediately they went along with James and John to the house of Simon and Andrew.
Simon's mother was lying down in bed. She had a fever. They told about her condition to Jesus.
So he walked over to her. He took her hand and helped her up. The spell was broken. After that, she started working for them.
That night, after sunset, people brought to Jesus all who were sick. They brought their sick children, everyone who was possessed by demons.
I gathered all the people in the place in front of the door.
Jesus healed many of them. They had all kinds of diseases. And he cast out many demons. But he did not allow them to speak, because they knew him. Jesus prayed in a quiet place.
It was very early in the morning, and the darkness was still very deep. Jesus got up and went out of the house. He went to a place where he could be alone. There he prayed.
Simon and his friends went to look for Jesus.
When they found him, they said to him, "Everyone is looking for you!"
Jesus said, "Let us go to the next place. I want to go to the nearby towns. I must preach there a lot. This is the reason I came."
He traveled throughout Galilee. He preached in their synagogues. He also cast out demons. Jesus heals a man with a skin disease.
A man with a skin disease came to the synagogue. He sat down in front, earnestly begging. He said, "If you are willing to make me clean, it is within your power."
Jesus was very much perplexed. He stretched out his hand and touched the man. "I am willing," he said, "to do it. Just say 'Come!'"
Now the illness has increased for him. Get well.
Jesus sent him away at once; and he warned the man severely.
He told me, "Don't tell anyone this, go and present yourself to the priest. Offer the sacrifices that Moses commanded. Then the priest and the people will witness that you are 'pure'."
But the man went out and began to tell it immediately. He spread the news to everyone. Thus, Jesus could no longer enter the country openly. He remained outside in lonely places. But people kept coming to him from everywhere.
Jesus heals a man who could not walk.
A few days later, Jesus entered Capernaum again. When the people heard that he had returned home,
A large crowd gathered, so much so that there was no more room for them, not even outside the door. And Jesus preached the word to them.
Four of those who came were carrying a man who could not walk.
But they couldn't get him to Jesus because of the crowd. So they dug an opening through the roof above Jesus. Then they lowered the man on his stretcher through the opening.
Jesus saw their faith. He said to the man, "Son, your sins are forgiven."
Some of the scholars of Islamic law were sitting there. They were thinking,
Why do these two speak like this? They are saying Satanic things! But God forgives sins!
Jesus knew what you were thinking. He said to them, "Why do you think such thoughts?"
Which is easier: to tell him, "Your sins are forgiven," or "Rise, take up your mat and walk"?
"We love you, you know that a human being has authority on earth to forgive sins." After that, Jesus spoke with the man who could not walk.
He told me, "Get up, take your mat, and go home."
The man got up and took his mattock. He walked away, everyone watching him. Everyone was amazed. They praised God and said, "We have never seen anything like this before!" Jesus chose Levi.
Again Jesus went to the seashore of the Sea of Galilee. A great crowd came to him. He began to teach them.
As he was walking, he saw Levi, the son of Alphaeus. Levi was sitting in the tax office. He said to him, "Follow me," Jesus. And Levi got up and followed him.
Later, Jesus was having dinner at Levi's house. He was joined by a group of tax collectors and "sinners" eating with him and the disciples. They were part of the larger group that was following Jesus.
There were some teachers of the law who were Pharisees. They saw Jesus eating with "sinners" and tax collectors. So they asked his disciples, "Why does he eat with tax collectors and 'sinners'?"
Jesus heard that. He said to them, "The sick don't need a doctor, but the sick do need one. I didn't come to take those who think they are righteous with God, I came to take sinners so that they would follow me."
The disciples of John and the Pharisees used to fast. The disciples of Jesus came to him and said, "Why do the disciples of John and the Pharisees fast, but your disciples do not fast?"
Jesus answered and said, "How can the guests of the bridegroom fast while he is with them? They cannot fast as long as he is with them."
But the time will come when the bridegroom will be taken from them. On that day they will fast from food.
People do not sew a new piece of cloth onto old clothes. If they did, the new piece would be distanced from the old one. This is how the tear becomes bigger.
People do not pour new wine into old wineskins. Otherwise, the new wine will burst the skins, and both the wine and the wineskins will be ruined. No, everyone puts new wine into new wineskins. Jesus is Lord of the Sabbath.
Jesus was walking with His disciples on a Sabbath in the wheat fields. And the disciples began to pluck the heads of grain and rub them with their hands.
The Pharisees said to Jesus: "Behold, this is a violation of the law regarding the Sabbath. What are they doing to act in this way, to make your disciples?"
Answer: "Have you not read what David did? He and his companions were hungry. They needed food."
There was a time when Abiathar was high priest. David entered the house of God and ate the holy bread. Only the priests were allowed to eat it. And David gave a lot to his men.
Then Jesus said to them, "The Sabbath was made for man, and not man for the Sabbath."
Here's why the human boy is even master of the Sabbath.
Healing on Saturday
Again Jesus went to the synagogue. There was a man who had a withered hand.
Some Pharisees were trying to find fault with Jesus. They were watching him closely. They wanted to see if he would heal a man on the Sabbath.
Jesus spoke to the man who had a withered and twisted hand. "Get up in front of everyone," he told him.
Then Jesus asked them, "What does the law say about what we should do on the Sabbath? Should we do good or evil? Should we save life or destroy it?" But no one answered him.
He saw Jesus around him with all anger. He was annoyed by their stubborness. Then He said to the man, "Stretch out your hand." He stretched it out, and his hand was restored as the other.
Then the Pharisees went out and started to plot with the Herodians against Jesus. The people were following Jesus.
Jesus walked to the Sea of Galilee with his disciples. A large crowd from Galilee followed him.
The people heard about everything Jesus had done. Large numbers of people came to see him. They came from Judea, Jerusalem, and Idumea. They came from the region east of the Jordan River. And they came from the area of Tyre and Sidon.
Due to the crowd, Jesus said to his disciples: "Prepare a small boat for me." This is so we don't stop people from gathering around him.
Jesus was healing many people. Therefore, the sick were pushing each other to touch him.
When the people who had evil spirits saw him, they fell down before him. And the spirits cried out, "You are the Son of God!"
But Jesus commanded them not to tell who he was. Jesus appoints the twelve disciples.
Jesus went up on a mountain. He called some people to come to him, and they came.
He appointed 12 of them and called them apostles. From then on, they would be with him. And he would send them to preach.
They have the power to cast out demons.
Jesus called the twelve. Simon was one of them. Jesus named him Peter.
James, the son of Zebedee, and his brother John. Jesus named them Boanerges. Boanerges means Sons of Thunder.
There were many other people, such as Andrew, Philip, Bartholomew, Matthew, Thomas, and James, the son of Alphaeus. There was also Thaddeus and Simon the Zealot.
Juda Iscariote was one of them, he too. He is the next one to hand Jesus over to his enemies. Jesus and Beelzebub
Jesus entered a house. The crowd gathered again. There were so many that Jesus and his disciples couldn't even eat.
His family heard the news. So they went to take care of him. They told him, "This guy is crazy."
There were some teachers of the law there. They had come from Jerusalem. They said, "He is controlled by Beelzebul! He is driving out demons by the power of the ruler of demons."
Jesus sat down with them and taught them by stories. He said to them, "How can Satan cast out Satan?"
If a kingdom is at war with itself, it cannot stand.
If a family breaks up, you can't stop it.
